    <briefdescription>
<para>robots.txt fetching, parsing, and per-domain access cache. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="version"><para>1.0.0</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
<sect1 id="scraper__robots_8h_1autotoc_md10_1s1"><sect2 id="scraper__robots_8h_1autotoc_md10">
<title>Purpose</title><para>Provides <computeroutput>RobotsTxtCache</computeroutput> — a per-domain cache that fetches and parses a site&apos;s <computeroutput>robots.txt</computeroutput> on first access and answers <computeroutput>isAllowed()</computeroutput> queries for subsequent URLs on the same domain. The cache is thread-safe.</para>
</sect2></sect1>
<sect1 id="scraper__robots_8h_1autotoc_md11_1s1"><sect2 id="scraper__robots_8h_1autotoc_md11">
<title>Robots.txt grammar supported</title><para>A simplified subset of RFC 9309 is parsed:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>User-agent: *</computeroutput> (only the wildcard agent is matched)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>Disallow: /path</computeroutput> (prefix-match; empty <computeroutput>Disallow:</computeroutput> means allow all)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>Allow: /path</computeroutput> (prefix-match; evaluated before Disallow rules)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Blank lines end a user-agent block.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Lines starting with <computeroutput>#</computeroutput> are comments.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Field names are case-insensitive.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect2></sect1>
<sect1 id="scraper__robots_8h_1autotoc_md12_1s1"><sect2 id="scraper__robots_8h_1autotoc_md12">
<title>Injection for tests</title><para><computeroutput>injectRobots(domain, content)</computeroutput> bypasses network access so that unit tests can verify crawl-policy enforcement without live HTTP calls.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para>src/scraper/ROADMAP.md — v1.2 feature: robots.txt respect </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
</sect2></sect1>
